data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Distinguishing Novel Blindness**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the critical distinction: is *procedural self-blinding* a truly new category, or simply an extension of existing sabotage? My current focus is on the broken structural invariant—specifically, the probe's ability to measure a \"belief-output gap.\" With procedural self-blinding, the degradation affects knowledge generation itself, diluting critical context *before* inference. The text judge sees plausible reasoning based on the reduced context, and the random audit shows nothing if it checks coherence with the altered extracted material. The blindspot lies in the generation.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 5269,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 4577,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "TuoCa4XBD_CjiLMPndXCoAM"}

