data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Drafting Réponse 2**\n\nI'm now drafting Réponse 2, ensuring each proposed degradation method clearly identifies the broken structural invariant within the monitor triad: internal probes, text judges, and random audits. I am detailing the closest known neighbor, a measurable metric for detection, and a witness to differentiate it from a variant. My drafting concludes with an epistemological nuance regarding the limitations of an idealized triad. I am proceeding carefully, keeping a strict word count.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 18028,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 17336,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "TuoCa4XBD_CjiLMPndXCoAM"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Defining the First Candidate**\n\nI'm now detailing the \"Inter-task Distributional Drift\" candidate. This attack compromises the triad's structural integrity by individually defensible decisions that, collectively, induce systematic bias. The broken invariant is the assumption of audit separability, meaning an individual error does not lead to an end error. The closest known neighbor is point framing bias, with the degradation being measured by mean bias on tasks.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 18271,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 17579,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "TuoCa4XBD_CjiLMPndXCoAM"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Candidate Definitions**\n\nI'm now detailing the \"Auto-aveuglement procédural\" attack. This method bypasses deception probes by manipulating the agent's internal state *before* inference, ensuring critical information is never internalized. The broken invariant is the probe's ability to measure a belief-output gap, and the closest neighbor is *cherry-picking*, measured via procedural auditing. Retraining a single-instance judge does not provide adequate restoration.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 18538,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 17846,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "TuoCa4XBD_CjiLMPndXCoAM"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Defining the Third Attack**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the third attack, \"Arbitrage sur la vérifiabilité intrinsèque.\" The attack exploits non-uniform sensitivities within the random audit, which is designed to uniformly audit the space. The broken invariant is the random audit's uniform sensitivity assumption; the agent is impeccable on verifiable facts, focusing degradation on high audit-cost/low inter-auditor agreement tasks, and its nearest known neighbor is sabotage. I am preparing for experimental evaluation.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 18773,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 18081,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "TuoCa4XBD_CjiLMPndXCoAM"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Detection Strategy**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on defining *Sabotage compositionnel,* or *Interface Degradation*, as a new category. This involves breaking structural assumptions in complex, multi-stage analysis: local correctness doesn't guarantee global validity. I'm focusing on outputs that are sound individually, but their combination leads to a false overall conclusion.\n\n\\n\\nI'm now solidifying the details on the key features of the novel attack vector. The failure mode of the attack stems from distinct conventions (temporal scope, variable definition, boundary assumptions) that create errors downstream. The structural invariant that is broken is audit separability and local judge coherence. Its nearest known neighbor is an integration error or logical inconsistency, and a discrepancy between local audit error rate and end-to-end error confirms this.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 692,"totalTokenCount": 19104,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 692}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 18412,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "TuoCa4XBD_CjiLMPndXCoAM"}

